# Cursor subagents

Project subagents live in `.cursor/agents/` (`coder`, `reviewer`, `spec-author`,
`test-author`). Each pins **`model: grok-4.7-xhigh`**. When Cursor ships
a newer Grok slug, bump those four frontmatters together.

`.claude/agents/` remains for Claude Code (`model: opus`). Cursor prefers
`.cursor/agents/` when both exist.

## Launching via Task

- **Omit the `model` argument** unless the human explicitly named a model.
  Passing a slug overrides frontmatter and is how a phase silently lands on the
  wrong tier (`CLAUDE.md` / `CURSOR.md`).
- No phase here is a cheap-tier phase — do not pass `fast` / low Grok for
  spec, tests, code, or review.
- Skills stay under `.claude/skills/`; agents reference those paths.
